For static analysis, it can be useful to recurse through function bodies. This can typically done with code of the form, for example:

```
recurse <- function(object, callback, ...) {
  callback(object, ...)
  for (i in seq_along(object))
    if (is.call(object[[i]]))
      recurse(object[[i]], callback, ...)
}
```

It would be useful (and slightly more performant) if we could iterate instead via:

```
recurse <- function(object, callback, ...) {
  callback(object, ...)
  for (el in object)
    if (is.call(el))
      recurse(el, callback, ...)
}
```

but unfortunately R doesn't accept language objects for iteration in a for loop, even though pairlists are accepted. E.g.

```
> data <- pairlist(as.symbol("rnorm"), 42)
> for (el in data) {
+   print(el)
+ }
rnorm
[1] 42
> 
> for (el in as.call(data)) {
+   print(el)
+ }
Error in for (el in as.call(data)) { : invalid for() loop sequence
```

If I understand correctly, it would be straightforward to allow this:

```
diff --git a/src/main/eval.c b/src/main/eval.c
index a0cf1966f5..73108a2fca 100644
--- a/src/main/eval.c
+++ b/src/main/eval.c
@@ -2835,6 +2835,7 @@ attribute_hidden SEXP do_for(SEXP call, SEXP op, SEXP args, SEXP rho)
            break;

        case LISTSXP:
+       case LANGSXP:
            /* make sure loop variable is not modified via other vars */
            ENSURE_NAMEDMAX(CAR(val));
            defineVar(sym, CAR(val), rho);
```

Perhaps related; I believe `lapply()` could also accept pairlists and language objects as-is, but those are currently coerced to R lists. That would still lead to an underlying implementation that iterates using indexes though, so I think the change for `for` loops would be more useful.

Here's a more complete version of the patch.

```
--- a/src/main/eval.c
+++ b/src/main/eval.c
@@ -2835,6 +2835,7 @@ attribute_hidden SEXP do_for(SEXP call, SEXP op, SEXP args, SEXP rho)
            break;

        case LISTSXP:
+       case LANGSXP:
            /* make sure loop variable is not modified via other vars */
            ENSURE_NAMEDMAX(CAR(val));
            defineVar(sym, CAR(val), rho);
@@ -7657,7 +7658,7 @@ static SEXP bcEval_loop(struct bcEval_locals *ploc)
 #endif
        if (isVector(seq))
          loopinfo->len = XLENGTH(seq);
-       else if (isList(seq) || isNull(seq))
+       else if (isList(seq) || isLanguage(seq))
          loopinfo->len = length(seq);
        else errorcall(GETCONST(constants, callidx),
                       _("invalid for() loop sequence"));
@@ -7788,6 +7789,7 @@ static SEXP bcEval_loop(struct bcEval_locals *ploc)
            ENSURE_NAMEDMAX(value);
            break;
          case LISTSXP:
+         case LANGSXP:
            value = CAR(seq);
            SET_FOR_LOOP_SEQ(CDR(seq));
            ENSURE_NAMEDMAX(value);
```
